# helixailabs.com — Apache directives
#
# 2026-08-24: retired the pre-migration documentation URLs.
#
# Two generations of docs were still being served publicly:
#   /HowTos/valence_docs.html    /HowTos/valence_guides.html   (git-tracked, redeployed every push)
#   /valence_docs.html           /valence_guides.html          (server-only; NOT in the repo, so
#                                                               deploy.ps1 could never see or fix them)
# All four returned HTTP 200 while claiming to match "Valence v1.4.5" — a version that was never
# released — and their navigation pointed at pages that 404. They had no inbound links from any
# current page, which is exactly why they survived every release pass untouched.
#
# The files are deleted. These redirects exist because the URLs may hold external links and search
# placement, and because the retired copy told readers (and any AI they pasted it into) to treat
# /valence_docs.html as the authoritative guide. A 301 sends that traffic to the real handbook
# instead of a 404.
#
# mod_alias Redirect is used rather than mod_rewrite: no RewriteEngine dependency, and the mapping
# is a plain one-to-one. Targets are percent-encoded because the live filenames contain spaces.

Redirect 301 /HowTos/valence_docs.html   /Valence%20-%20Docs.html
Redirect 301 /HowTos/valence_guides.html /Valence%20-%20Guides.html
Redirect 301 /valence_docs.html          /Valence%20-%20Docs.html
Redirect 301 /valence_guides.html        /Valence%20-%20Guides.html

# 2026-08-24: retired the standalone MCP setup guides (dated 2026-03-14). Same class as
# the pages above - server-only, absent from the repo, no inbound link from any current
# page - so deploy.ps1 could not manage them either.
#
# These point at the HANDBOOK, not at /Valence - Guides.html: the Guides page does not
# mention MCP at all, so sending someone asking about MCP setup there would be a dead end
# dressed as a redirect. Docs, Privacy & Licensing and Tech Specs are where MCP is covered.
Redirect 301 /Guides/mcp-brave-search.html  /Valence%20-%20Docs.html
Redirect 301 /Guides/mcp-github.html        /Valence%20-%20Docs.html
Redirect 301 /Guides/mcp-nodejs-setup.html  /Valence%20-%20Docs.html

# 2026-09-06: site v2 ships a styled /404.html at the site root.
#
# This directive is INERT on the current host and is kept deliberately.
# GoDaddy shared hosting overrides ErrorDocument at the server level: tested with
# both a path and a literal string, and both are ignored - a missing URL returns a
# bare 13-byte "404 Not Found" either way, while the mod_alias Redirects in this
# same file work, so the file is definitely being read. The custom error page has
# to be set through cPanel's "Error Pages" tool instead, which is browser-only.
#
# The line stays because it is correct everywhere else (GitHub Pages serves
# 404.html automatically; a normal Apache honours this), so if the site ever moves
# off GoDaddy the styled page starts working with no change needed here.
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html

# 2026-09-06: URLs the SHIPPED app links to that returned 404 on the live site.
# These are not old marketing URLs - they are live buttons inside Valence, so
# every user who clicks them today lands on an error page. Found by extracting
# every helixailabs.com URL from the app source and curling each one.
#
# Two of the three are pure case mismatches against redirects that already exist
# above: mod_alias Redirect is case-sensitive, and the app links "Valence_Guides"
# and "/guides/" while the rules above only cover "valence_guides" and "/Guides/".
#
#   Settings > About > "Help & Guides"        -> the Guides page it means
#   Settings > MCP > Node.js setup guide      -> Docs, matching the /Guides/ rule above
Redirect 301 /Valence_Guides.html            /Valence%20-%20Guides.html
Redirect 301 /guides/mcp-nodejs-setup.html   /Valence%20-%20Docs.html

# Settings > Memory > "HIVE Coming Soon - Learn More". There is no HIVE page on
# the site and Docs does not mention it, so sending this to Docs would be a dead
# end dressed as a redirect - the same mistake the MCP note above avoids. The
# home page is the honest destination until HIVE has a page of its own. The real
# fix is in the app: SettingsModalComponent.js hiveLearnMoreBtn should not link
# to a page that does not exist.
Redirect 301 /hive_explore.html              /
